Subject: ath11k: flush wmi_mgmt_tx_work before waiting for mgmt tx completion

Under the single-executor native Linux shim (lx_rt.c), ordinary workqueues
without LX_WQ_IO_COMPLETION are deferred while any mutex (such as mac80211's
wiphy->mtx) is held unless explicitly flushed via flush_work().

During disconnect / network switch, mac80211 transmits a DEAUTH frame
(queuing ar->wmi_mgmt_tx_work on ab->workqueue_aux and incrementing
ar->num_pending_mgmt_tx) and immediately invokes drv_flush() while still
holding wiphy->mtx. Without flushing ar->wmi_mgmt_tx_work first,
ath11k_mac_flush_tx_complete() spins for the full 5 s ATH11K_FLUSH_TIMEOUT
per flush call (10-15 s total), causing wpa_supplicant control timeouts and
join retries.

--- a/mac.c
+++ b/mac.c
@@ -8659,6 +8659,9 @@ static void ath11k_mac_op_flush(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *v
 	if (drop)
 		return;
 
+	if (!mutex_is_locked(&ar->conf_mutex))
+		flush_work(&ar->wmi_mgmt_tx_work);
+
 	ath11k_mac_flush_tx_complete(ar);
 }
 
